# 24h granite-plate test's raw 20Hz stream (2026-09-27): 709MB, well over
# GitHub's 100MB per-file limit (gzip only gets it to ~140MB, still over) --
# Testing/README.md's "commit the raw CSV" convention doesn't scale to a
# 24h/20Hz capture the way it does for shorter tests. findings.md/setup.md/
# the generated graphs ARE committed; this one raw file stays local-only
# until the project sets up Git LFS (not done as of this exclusion -- a
# repo-level decision with its own storage-quota tradeoffs, left for the
# user rather than made unilaterally). If a future test produces a
# similarly oversized CSV, add it here explicitly too rather than widening
# this pattern -- most tests' CSVs are small enough to commit normally and
# should stay tracked.
Testing/2026-09-27_24hr_granite_plate_test/data/granite_24hr.csv

# host unit-test binaries (tests/Makefile builds these; sources are tracked)
tests/test_math_crc
tests/test_txframe
tests/test_transfer
tests/*.exe
tests/test_math_phasor
tests/test_math_window
tests/test_math_displacement
tests/test_math_quality
tests/test_golden_displacement

# recorded test data the host tests replay (tests/data/README.md) -- must be tracked
!tests/data/*.bin

# bench-test data above the 5 MB policy limit (Testing/README.md, "Data policy"); see Testing/large_files.py
Testing/*/data/large/
Testing/2026-09-30_bulk_adc_30s_interval/analysis/quality_tune.npz
